# OpenSocrates for Google Antigravity

This package provides the experimental, explicit-skill Antigravity boundary
for OpenSocrates {{PRODUCT_VERSION}}. It exposes one `opensocrates` Agent Skill
backed by {{METHOD_COUNT}} internal reasoning-system references.

When the explicit skill reads a generated method, that complete procedure
begins with three authored teacher questions for the active agent to settle
without unnecessarily interviewing the user. This is content delivered by the
skill, not hidden hook injection.

## Support level

- Explicit Agent Skill invocation: **supported by the documented plugin and
  skills contract**; an authenticated live invocation receipt is still pending.
- Automatic per-prompt selection: **not included**.
- Native hook delivery: **not claimed**.
- Additional model calls: **none**. The package does not consume a separate
  Google AI Pro request to classify each prompt.
- Antigravity Desktop/IDE and public marketplace distribution: **not claimed**.

The package contains no launcher, native runtime, executable, hook definition,
MCP server, telemetry, or background service. It is a content-only plugin.

## Installation contract

Antigravity documents global plugins under
`~/.gemini/config/plugins/<plugin-name>/`. The `plugin.json` file is the
required plugin marker, and skills live under `skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`.
The OpenSocrates installer owns only the `opensocrates` directory and refuses
to replace a directory without its exact ownership marker.

After installation, start a new Antigravity CLI session and open `/skills` to
confirm discovery. Invoke the `opensocrates` skill explicitly for judgment
work. No automatic hook participation occurs in this version.

See Google's [Agent Skills documentation](https://antigravity.google/docs/skills)
and [Plugins documentation](https://antigravity.google/docs/ide/plugins).

